== S1  the single-pair chart obstruction (per-pair principles cannot exclude the mixed assignment)
PASS C1  [identity] actT reflY is ipW-orthogonal and an involution, symbolic
PASS C2  [identity] actT reflY (prodState x y) = prodState x (reflY y), symbolic: it maps SEP onto SEP
PASS C3  [identity] a^T (actT reflY w) b = a^T w (homMap reflY b), symbolic, and homMap reflY preserves the Lorentz form: actT reflY maps maxCone onto maxCone
PASS C4  [identity] cnotTw = actT reflY . cnot . actT reflY is the N-CLASS gate with locals (I, reflY, I, reflY), symbolic
PASS C5  [identity] ipW F (actT reflY w) = ipW (actT reflY F) w, symbolic: dualW twin = actT reflY (dualW Q3) = twin
NOTE [written] C.W  -- let P be any predicate of the data of ONE pair (its cone, its gate, its four locals) that is invariant under transport by the ipW-orthogonal, SEP- and maxCone-preserving involution actT reflY (cone K -> its image, gate N -> actT reflY . N . actT reflY, locals transformed by the chart rule). Self-duality K = dualW K, its two halves, homogeneity, symmetric-cone (Jordan) structure, closedness, admissibility and gate invariance are all such predicates (C1-C5). Then P(Q3, cnot, I, I, I, I) iff P(twin, cnotTw, I, reflY, I, reflY). The model M_tok = (Q3, Q3, Q3, twin) with gates (cnot, cnot, cnot, cnotTw) therefore satisfies every conjunction of such predicates that the quantum data M_Q satisfy, while FCC fails there at -1/8 (s1 A3). No conjunction of chart-invariant single-pair predicates implies FCC. This complements AUDIT-C's narrowed B3 (three-pair conditions on cones and gate maps): for one pair, conditions may read the locals as well.

